  "english": "20. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [bk]: \"Christ is risen\" (ZKristos yaryav), and Morning [Hymn].\n\n27. Sunday. Tone 3 [DZ]. Seventh [Sunday]. Feast of the Discovery of the Cross.\n\n29. Tuesday. Tone 4 [GZ]. [Feast of] the Saints Hyperichius and Severian, etc. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 1 [ak]: \"Holy God the Creator\" (Soorp astvats ararich).\n\n30. Wednesday. Tone 4 [GK]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 4 [dz]: \"God of our fathers, who saved us\" (Hartsn merots astvats vor abretsooter). See the others according to the order in the First [book].\n[Scribal / printing noise]\n\nNovember.\n\n2. Saturday. Tone 1 [AZ]. All Saints, old and new, etc.\n\n3. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Eighth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ak]: \"The risen Lord\" (Yarootsyal tern) and \"The wondrous angel\" (Skancheli hreshtakn).\n\n10. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Ninth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [adz]: \"With the women\" (End ganaysn), to the end.\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 4 [DK]. Tenth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [dk]: \"Thy angel, O Lord\" (Hreshtag ko ter), to the end. Carnival of the Advent Fast [Yisnakats].\n\n18. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Fast of Advent [Yisnakats]. Hymn of the Fathers: \"Who in all things didst reveal\" (Vor yamenayni tsootser).\n\n21. Thursday. Tone 2 [BK]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the three-year-old Holy Mother of God [into the Temple].\n\n24. Sunday. Tone 4 [DZ]. First [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 1 [ak]: \"Beginningless Word\" (Ansgizpn band). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [dz]: \"Awful\" (Ahadin) and \"Thou who art above\" (Vor i verd es).\n\n25. Monday. Tone 4 [DK]. [Feast of] Saints Julian and Basiliscus, and Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and the martyr Adeodatus [Astvatsatoor]. Hymn of the Fathers [of Martyrs]: \"They who the torments\" (Ork ztanjans).\n\nDecember.\n\n1. Sunday. Tone 4 [GK]. Second [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 3 [bdz]: \"Thou who art King\" (Vor tagavorat es). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [gk]: \"Assuming and our\" (Aryal yev mer).\n\n2. Monday. Tone 4 [DZ]. [Feast of] Bishop Gennarius, and the soldier Mercurius, and Yakovik [James] and Irava-par [Justus].\n\n3. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DK]. [Feast of] Minas, Hermogenes, etc. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 4 [dz]: \"They who hoped\" (Yoosatsyalpn).\n\n8. Sunday. Tone 4 [GZ]. Third [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 2 [bk]: \"Beginningless God\" (Ansgizpn astvats). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [gz]: \"Glorified is Thy\" (Paravorval e ko). Carnival of Saint James [Surb Hakob].\n\n9. Monday. Tone 4 [GK]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin.\n\n15. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 4 [gz]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paravorval vordi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [bk]: \"The women forestalled\" (Gantphetsin ganaykn).\n\n18. Wednesday. Tone 4 [DZ]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 4 [dk]: \"Of our fathers\" (Hartsn merots).\n\n22. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 4 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhayavitean). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [bdz]: \"In the tomb\" (I gerezman), and \"They came to the tomb\" (Yegin i gerezman), and \"The voice of good tidings\" (Dzayn avetavor), and \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zvartchatsan).\n\n23. Monday. Tone 2 [BK]. [Feast of] David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Hymn of the Fathers [of Martyrs]: \"Only-begotten Son of God\" (Miatsin vordi astvatsots). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [ak]: \"Wonderful resurrection\" (Hrashali zyaro). Carnival of the Nativity Fast.\n\n30. Monday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Hymn of the Fathers, Tone 1 [ak]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God of our fathers\" (Orhneal es ter astvats hartsn merots).\n\nJanuary.\n\n1. Wednesday. Tone 4 [GZ]. Fast. Hymn of the Fathers [of Penitence], Tone 1 [adz]: \"The children sang\" (Yerkein mangoonkn).\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Seventh [Sunday]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ our God.",
